  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{d y}{d x}=y+3 \\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{y+3}=d x$\n$\\ln (y+3)=x+c$\n$x=0 \\Rightarrow y=2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\ln 5=0+c$\n$c=\\ln 5$\n$\\ln (y+3)=x+\\ln 5$\n$y+3=e^{x+\\ln 5} \\Rightarrow y+3=e^{\\ln 2+\\ln 5}$\n$y+3=10 \\Rightarrow y=7$",
